1
00:00:01,555 --> 00:00:04,224
Oh no, I'm gonna be late!

2
00:00:04,307 --> 00:00:06,476
Wait. What did I just say?

3
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:09,354
That phrase… It sounded so familiar.

4
00:00:12,024 --> 00:00:13,984
She's the one
who went running out into the street

5
00:00:14,067 --> 00:00:15,485
right in front of us.

6
00:00:16,903 --> 00:00:18,989
ONE WAY STREET

7
00:00:19,072 --> 00:00:21,408
Please, miss,
be more aware of your surroundings.

8
00:00:23,618 --> 00:00:25,620
Let us give you a ride to school.

9
00:00:30,208 --> 00:00:32,794
It seems like a pretty expensive car.

10
00:00:35,088 --> 00:00:37,966
Hey, um, I'm really sorry
that I made you late.

11
00:00:38,675 --> 00:00:40,177
Having a couple of tardies?

12
00:00:40,927 --> 00:00:44,056
That won't affect my report card.
I'm an excellent student.

13
00:00:44,556 --> 00:00:47,517
Anyway,
why would a rich kid like him

14
00:00:47,601 --> 00:00:49,227
go to a public school?

15
00:00:49,311 --> 00:00:52,064
He's good-looking
but I haven't seen him before.

16
00:00:52,647 --> 00:00:54,483
Well, you must be ecstatic.

17
00:00:55,275 --> 00:00:58,987
I mean, getting the chance
to ride to school with me and everything.

18
00:00:59,571 --> 00:01:01,073
You should be grateful.

19
00:01:04,076 --> 00:01:06,912
Hang on, Anzu,
don't punch him in the face.

20
00:01:06,995 --> 00:01:10,874
Hold it in. This all happened
because I was being careless.

21
00:01:12,209 --> 00:01:14,878
Oh. Both Kazuki and Saki messaged me.

22
00:01:14,961 --> 00:01:15,796
TSUKASA: YOU GOOD?

23
00:01:15,879 --> 00:01:17,089
I should respond.

24
00:01:17,172 --> 00:01:19,382
I GOT IN A MINOR ACCIDENT,
BUT I'M OKAY.

25
00:02:50,348 --> 00:02:53,768
#7: WHAT A STRONG PERSONALITY

26
00:02:57,022 --> 00:02:58,899
Great, just in time for break.

27
00:03:01,276 --> 00:03:03,862
Uh, this is me right here.

28
00:03:04,446 --> 00:03:06,907
You exchanged contacts
with Tsuchiya, right?

29
00:03:06,990 --> 00:03:07,824
Hmm?

30
00:03:07,908 --> 00:03:09,951
-My name is Tsuchiya.
-Oh, yeah.

31
00:03:10,452 --> 00:03:13,371
I'll be in touch at a later day.
You just wait.

32
00:03:14,289 --> 00:03:16,249
And enjoy dreaming about me.

33
00:03:17,959 --> 00:03:20,462
Seriously?
There's still more to talk about?

34
00:03:22,172 --> 00:03:23,715
Hmm?

35
00:03:23,798 --> 00:03:24,633
Oh…

36
00:03:24,716 --> 00:03:28,386
Anzu! Why did you arrive
with Mr. Hijiri Koganei?

37
00:03:28,470 --> 00:03:29,304
Mister?

38
00:03:29,387 --> 00:03:31,890
Anzu, are… are you sure
that you're not hurt?

39
00:03:31,973 --> 00:03:33,308
Yeah, thank you, Saki.

40
00:03:33,391 --> 00:03:35,352
You are so lucky!

41
00:03:35,435 --> 00:03:38,063
You got hit by Mr. Hijiri's car.

42
00:03:38,146 --> 00:03:39,814
Why do you keep saying "Mister"?

43
00:03:39,898 --> 00:03:40,815
What do you mean?

44
00:03:40,899 --> 00:03:43,777
He's Mr. Hijiri Koganei,
the rich star from Class 8!

45
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:46,154
He is like a prince.
He even has his own fan club.

46
00:03:46,238 --> 00:03:47,072
PRINCE HIJIRI

47
00:03:47,781 --> 00:03:48,907
I see…

48
00:03:49,407 --> 00:03:51,076
I mean, it seems obvious,

49
00:03:51,159 --> 00:03:54,579
but, this has got to be
another one of their setups!

50
00:03:54,663 --> 00:03:56,539
-I got to get up…
-And insert!

51
00:03:56,623 --> 00:03:59,459
-I'll be late…
-Now she'll be running really late!

52
00:03:59,542 --> 00:04:00,877
-Hosshi!
-Anzu!

53
00:04:00,961 --> 00:04:02,087
Oh!

54
00:04:02,170 --> 00:04:05,173
-Are you okay? We heard you got hit!
-Anzu, I was worried about you.

55
00:04:06,174 --> 00:04:07,467
Hayami! Oh gosh!

56
00:04:07,550 --> 00:04:10,553
-You're not hurt at all, are you?
-Nope. I'm all good.

57
00:04:13,098 --> 00:04:15,600
I bet you were rushing
and ran into the street.

58
00:04:15,684 --> 00:04:16,810
Yeah.

59
00:04:16,893 --> 00:04:19,521
Still, I really think
you should go to the hospital.

60
00:04:19,604 --> 00:04:21,273
The car barely hit me, though.

61
00:04:21,356 --> 00:04:23,525
Hosshi, you and Hayami are friends?

62
00:04:23,608 --> 00:04:24,943
Nice!

63
00:04:25,026 --> 00:04:27,988
He's, um, he's an "old friend,"
quote unquote.

64
00:04:28,071 --> 00:04:29,406
Let's go.

65
00:04:29,489 --> 00:04:31,783
Let me know if anything starts hurting,
all right?

66
00:04:31,866 --> 00:04:33,285
Okay, thanks.

67
00:04:34,536 --> 00:04:36,538
This is so incredibly unfair,

68
00:04:36,621 --> 00:04:37,580
I can't even…

69
00:04:37,664 --> 00:04:40,709
Both of those heartthrobs are just
so worried about you.

70
00:04:40,792 --> 00:04:44,087
Well, actually,
Kazuki wasn't worried about me at all.

71
00:04:47,090 --> 00:04:50,010
A FEW DAYS LATER.

72
00:04:51,011 --> 00:04:52,971
Maybe I'm a little early.

73
00:04:56,099 --> 00:04:59,102
Would this coming Saturday
work for you?

74
00:05:00,270 --> 00:05:02,397
What else is left to go over?

75
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:09,529
You're extremely early.

76
00:05:10,905 --> 00:05:14,034
You wanted to see me so bad
you've been waiting here since last night?

77
00:05:15,577 --> 00:05:18,038
You really are something else, aren't you?

78
00:05:18,121 --> 00:05:20,915
Oh yeah, I've been waiting all night.

79
00:05:20,999 --> 00:05:23,543
Held strong,
like I was defending the Alamo.

80
00:05:24,544 --> 00:05:25,879
Whatever.

81
00:05:25,962 --> 00:05:28,256
What's with the peasant look
you've got on?

82
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:30,925
How could you even stand
next to me dressed like that?

83
00:05:31,009 --> 00:05:32,344
Are you trying to insult me?

84
00:05:35,805 --> 00:05:39,434
I humbly apologize.
I'm just a low-born villager NPC

85
00:05:39,517 --> 00:05:41,895
in a game, repeating the same line
over and over again.

86
00:05:41,978 --> 00:05:42,812
VILLAGER A

87
00:05:43,396 --> 00:05:45,440
Whatever.

88
00:05:46,149 --> 00:05:47,067
-Get in.
-Huh?

89
00:05:50,153 --> 00:05:53,073
You lack sincerity.

90
00:05:53,782 --> 00:05:57,577
With all my attention,
you'll be our school's Cinderella.

91
00:05:58,661 --> 00:06:01,831
Wanted:
Someone to translate for this guy.

92
00:06:04,918 --> 00:06:06,002
Well…

93
00:06:14,052 --> 00:06:17,931
-What the heck am I doing here?
-Aah…

94
00:06:18,807 --> 00:06:20,934
Hmm. Now you're decent.

95
00:06:21,434 --> 00:06:23,853
And now I wanna know what's happening.

96
00:06:25,939 --> 00:06:28,066
Get her some flat shoes.

97
00:06:28,149 --> 00:06:29,734
Why are you unnecessarily tall?

98
00:06:29,818 --> 00:06:32,195
Maybe I should give you
some of my height, then.

99
00:06:34,406 --> 00:06:37,158
-Okay, let's go to lunch.
-Huh? Whoa, wait, what?

100
00:06:37,242 --> 00:06:39,285
Go to lunch, why?

101
00:06:41,121 --> 00:06:43,206
I'm really pushed for time here.

102
00:06:43,289 --> 00:06:45,708
-Tell me what's going on!
-We're doing French.

103
00:06:45,792 --> 00:06:48,211
I don't need lunch!

104
00:06:49,295 --> 00:06:52,841
I don't get why you think it's okay
to make me over like that!

105
00:06:53,425 --> 00:06:54,884
It's entirely your fault

106
00:06:55,468 --> 00:06:58,346
for showing up on a date with me
dressed like a poor being.

107
00:06:58,930 --> 00:07:00,598
What are you talking about, date?

108
00:07:00,682 --> 00:07:03,059
Aren't we meeting 'cause I got hit?

109
00:07:03,143 --> 00:07:04,269
No need to play dumb.

110
00:07:04,894 --> 00:07:07,897
You purposefully got hit
in order to get closer to me, right?

111
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,691
Huh?

112
00:07:12,026 --> 00:07:14,904
Cars are legally at fault
when they hit pedestrians.

113
00:07:14,988 --> 00:07:18,366
You took advantage of that
so you could go out with me, didn't you?

114
00:07:18,450 --> 00:07:21,161
You actually think
that I staged the accident?

115
00:07:21,244 --> 00:07:23,746
-Oh, did you not?
-Not at all, no!

116
00:07:23,830 --> 00:07:25,498
Idiots like that exist?

117
00:07:25,582 --> 00:07:28,042
It's happened countless times
since preschool.

118
00:07:28,126 --> 00:07:29,544
So several exist, then.

119
00:07:29,627 --> 00:07:32,380
Tsuchiya's driver's license is
on a permanent watchlist now.

120
00:07:32,464 --> 00:07:33,923
It was suspended once too.

121
00:07:34,007 --> 00:07:36,926
You poor thing.
I'm really, really sorry!

122
00:07:37,802 --> 00:07:40,638
Anyway, I'm not one of those girls, and I,

123
00:07:40,722 --> 00:07:42,765
I can't accept these clothes.

124
00:07:42,849 --> 00:07:43,933
I'll pay for them.

125
00:07:44,434 --> 00:07:46,769
Nine hundred dollars, just for the dress.

126
00:07:47,770 --> 00:07:49,689
Is it made out of an ancient relic silk
or something?

127
00:07:49,772 --> 00:07:50,857
YOU OBTAINED ANCIENT THREADS!

128
00:07:50,940 --> 00:07:52,275
Whatever.

129
00:07:52,358 --> 00:07:55,320
Intentional or no,
it was still an accident.

130
00:07:56,446 --> 00:07:59,741
You received clothes and you're also
about to have lunch with me.

131
00:08:00,325 --> 00:08:02,494
Think of it as a peasant's godsend.

132
00:08:06,372 --> 00:08:07,957
Mr. Tsuchiya, please stop.

133
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:11,669
What now?

134
00:08:11,753 --> 00:08:13,963
I feel bad
that you did all of this for me.

135
00:08:14,464 --> 00:08:17,383
Whoa? Huh?

136
00:08:18,218 --> 00:08:20,512
I'm not at all interested in you.

137
00:08:21,721 --> 00:08:24,349
So there's no need for us
to waste each other's time.

138
00:08:25,725 --> 00:08:26,684
See ya.

139
00:08:29,604 --> 00:08:33,233
Being manipulated
by an extremely full of himself rich kid

140
00:08:33,316 --> 00:08:34,150
is really annoying,

141
00:08:34,234 --> 00:08:37,320
especially when he's got
a stuck-up attitude like that.

142
00:08:37,403 --> 00:08:39,531
But the most frustrating thing is

143
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:43,284
he actually thought
I was one of those idiots

144
00:08:43,368 --> 00:08:45,912
who would stage an accident for a date!

145
00:08:47,747 --> 00:08:51,251
I belong
to a warrior race that forges its way down

146
00:08:51,334 --> 00:08:54,337
the exact opposite path of life
every single day!

147
00:08:57,632 --> 00:09:01,177
Damn, my pits are sweating
all over this 900-dollar dress.

148
00:09:01,261 --> 00:09:03,680
THIS IS A ROMANTIC ANIME

149
00:09:05,765 --> 00:09:09,394
She has no interest in me?

150
00:09:15,525 --> 00:09:17,068
HIJIRI LOVE

151
00:09:17,151 --> 00:09:19,821
That's not good. Mr. Hijiri looks sad.

152
00:09:20,321 --> 00:09:22,532
But he looks so fragile and beautiful.

153
00:09:25,118 --> 00:09:25,952
Huh?

154
00:09:27,161 --> 00:09:28,580
Hijiri Koganei.

155
00:09:28,663 --> 00:09:31,207
Uh, it's you.

156
00:09:31,791 --> 00:09:34,544
Address me respectfully. That was rude.

157
00:09:34,627 --> 00:09:36,838
Are you kidding me?

158
00:09:36,921 --> 00:09:39,882
What do you want anyway?

159
00:09:39,966 --> 00:09:42,427
Trying to make up
for being rude the other day?

160
00:09:42,510 --> 00:09:45,555
I dry-cleaned the clothes,
so I just wanted to return them to you.

161
00:09:45,638 --> 00:09:46,639
Goodbye.

162
00:09:51,603 --> 00:09:53,479
She certainly left in a hurry

163
00:09:53,563 --> 00:09:56,524
after going out of her way
to return the gifts I gave her.

164
00:09:58,568 --> 00:10:01,237
There's no need
to worry about that peasant.

165
00:10:01,821 --> 00:10:04,824
But the way she's been giving me
all of that attitude…

166
00:10:07,577 --> 00:10:08,953
I don't like it one bit.

167
00:10:11,289 --> 00:10:14,083
Tsuchiya, I need something investigated.

168
00:10:19,631 --> 00:10:21,633
Junta, you're chipper.

169
00:10:21,716 --> 00:10:24,636
Wednesday means no club,
so I get to walk home with you.

170
00:10:24,719 --> 00:10:26,387
Oh, okay, I see.

171
00:10:26,471 --> 00:10:28,222
Kazuki has work today, right?

172
00:10:28,306 --> 00:10:30,558
Yeah. What should we do for dinner?

173
00:10:31,559 --> 00:10:34,145
It might be terrible,
but I can make us something.

174
00:10:34,646 --> 00:10:36,648
Really? You would? I'll eat it!

175
00:10:38,232 --> 00:10:40,693
You know, maybe I should learn
how to cook myself.

176
00:10:40,777 --> 00:10:42,528
I only know how to make ramen.

177
00:10:43,029 --> 00:10:45,031
You should just focus on your baseball.

178
00:10:45,657 --> 00:10:48,368
He's such a good guy
compared to that other one.

179
00:10:48,451 --> 00:10:52,246
I hope Junta finds happiness
with someone he truly loves.

180
00:10:52,330 --> 00:10:55,833
But for that to happen,
I really need to do something about them.

181
00:10:55,917 --> 00:10:57,043
Anzu!

182
00:10:57,627 --> 00:11:00,129
I wanna come too! Can I come for dinner?

183
00:11:00,213 --> 00:11:02,048
Maybe I should just give her
a quick death.

184
00:11:02,131 --> 00:11:03,549
Honestly, how dare you?

185
00:11:04,133 --> 00:11:06,344
Why send such a ridiculous character?

186
00:11:06,427 --> 00:11:08,137
There's no way I'd fall for him!

187
00:11:08,221 --> 00:11:11,557
Oh, when I'm in this form,
everybody can see and hear us.

188
00:11:13,685 --> 00:11:17,230
Well, I'm not a very good cook,
so you should probably just go home.

189
00:11:17,313 --> 00:11:19,565
-Not letting go of that grip, then?
-Hmm?

190
00:11:21,734 --> 00:11:22,568
Uh…

191
00:11:22,652 --> 00:11:24,153
Huh?

192
00:11:25,238 --> 00:11:26,572
Anzu Hoshino.

193
00:11:27,156 --> 00:11:28,199
Not him.

194
00:11:28,783 --> 00:11:32,203
You're the first woman to say
that you have no interest in me at all.

195
00:11:33,037 --> 00:11:34,205
I'm intrigued.

196
00:11:35,123 --> 00:11:37,959
Just know
that I'll steal your heart eventually.

197
00:11:38,751 --> 00:11:40,878
Heh.

198
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:46,259
-Aren't you starving?
-Mm-hm.

199
00:11:46,342 --> 00:11:49,262
-Oh, jeez. My stomach just rumbled…
-Goodness. Such a cramped place.

200
00:11:49,345 --> 00:11:52,515
-Oh! So, Junta…
-I'm sure it is for you, Mr. Prince.

201
00:11:52,598 --> 00:11:54,892
-By the way, who are these two?
-Huh?

202
00:11:54,976 --> 00:11:57,061
My business is only with Hoshino.

203
00:11:58,771 --> 00:12:00,648
I'm Riri, Anzu's cousin.

204
00:12:01,149 --> 00:12:04,402
And this is one of her oldest friends
from childhood, Junta.

205
00:12:04,485 --> 00:12:07,655
The three of us will be having dinner
together tonight.

206
00:12:07,739 --> 00:12:09,490
You can actually leave now.

207
00:12:10,324 --> 00:12:11,492
So…

208
00:12:12,076 --> 00:12:14,746
What's this business?
Some more lame stuff?

209
00:12:15,580 --> 00:12:17,081
Tsuchiya.

210
00:12:17,165 --> 00:12:18,040
Yes, sir.

211
00:12:20,209 --> 00:12:23,004
-Huh? Hmm…
-Miss Hoshino, this is for you.

212
00:12:25,590 --> 00:12:26,507
Huh?

213
00:12:27,133 --> 00:12:29,510
It's a Skitch! And a VR headset!

214
00:12:30,261 --> 00:12:32,722
The chocolates are all fancy brands!

215
00:12:36,225 --> 00:12:38,102
-And that's not all, miss.
-Huh?

216
00:12:49,113 --> 00:12:51,949
Destruction level: severe.

217
00:12:53,951 --> 00:12:57,038
Well, you appear
to be satisfied with my gifts.

218
00:12:57,121 --> 00:12:59,040
That came out of nowhere.

219
00:12:59,123 --> 00:13:02,627
Did he actually feel bad
about me getting upset?

220
00:13:03,127 --> 00:13:07,006
Along with great elegance
and my appearance which exudes charm,

221
00:13:08,132 --> 00:13:11,302
I have the financial power
to make your every wish come true.

222
00:13:13,721 --> 00:13:15,681
You're interested in me now, right?

223
00:13:15,765 --> 00:13:18,059
Oh, so it's that kind of scenario.

224
00:13:18,643 --> 00:13:21,521
Tell me, how did you find out
about my favorite things?

225
00:13:21,604 --> 00:13:23,272
Anything's possible for me.

226
00:13:23,356 --> 00:13:24,941
No, an actual answer.

227
00:13:26,526 --> 00:13:30,363
It really bothered you when I said
I wasn't interested in you, didn't it?

228
00:13:33,032 --> 00:13:35,076
-Well, guess what? Hey!
-Stop right there!

229
00:13:35,159 --> 00:13:38,579
Anzu, hon, I just need
a quick word with you for a second!

230
00:13:41,666 --> 00:13:45,336
I know that we confiscated
your three greatest desires,

231
00:13:45,419 --> 00:13:48,589
but it would be very rude
of you to reject his gifts.

232
00:13:48,673 --> 00:13:50,967
I will allow 'em,

233
00:13:51,050 --> 00:13:53,594
but here's the catch for accepting them!

234
00:13:53,678 --> 00:13:55,304
What, are you serious?

235
00:13:55,388 --> 00:13:56,597
You can only keep 'em

236
00:13:56,681 --> 00:14:00,059
if you allow a relationship
to develop with Hijiri Koganei.

237
00:14:04,939 --> 00:14:06,983
If I start dating him…

238
00:14:08,192 --> 00:14:11,279
…I can enjoy all those gifts right now.

239
00:14:16,784 --> 00:14:19,287
What are those two
talking about out there?

240
00:14:19,370 --> 00:14:21,080
Who… who knows?

241
00:14:23,124 --> 00:14:26,085
Um, your name was Koganei?

242
00:14:26,168 --> 00:14:27,670
That's informal and rude.

243
00:14:27,753 --> 00:14:30,548
Oh, sorry, Mr. Koganei.

244
00:14:30,631 --> 00:14:33,801
I heard about the accident
with Anzu and everything.

245
00:14:34,886 --> 00:14:37,054
But, um, well, do you, um…

246
00:14:37,972 --> 00:14:41,058
Anzu, uh, do you like her?

247
00:14:43,644 --> 00:14:44,645
Like her?

248
00:14:46,063 --> 00:14:49,066
That's not an emotion
I'd feel for anyone at all.

249
00:14:49,734 --> 00:14:52,570
That's an emotion
everyone else feels for me.

250
00:14:53,404 --> 00:14:54,572
Right.

251
00:14:54,655 --> 00:14:58,326
But Hoshino's stated
that she has absolutely no interest in me.

252
00:14:59,118 --> 00:15:00,494
It's a serious matter.

253
00:15:00,578 --> 00:15:03,581
I see.
That's why you're doing all this.

254
00:15:05,166 --> 00:15:08,961
Just so you know, Anzu won't become
your friend just because…

255
00:15:09,712 --> 00:15:11,547
you're rich or you're good-looking.

256
00:15:13,174 --> 00:15:14,050
Hmm?

257
00:15:16,177 --> 00:15:19,513
You're completely clueless
about humans.

258
00:15:20,181 --> 00:15:23,768
Setting up forced encounters
and messing with emotions,

259
00:15:23,851 --> 00:15:26,103
now luring me in with my desires.

260
00:15:29,357 --> 00:15:30,483
I'm no fool.

261
00:15:33,152 --> 00:15:33,986
Oh.

262
00:15:34,820 --> 00:15:37,990
-Please leave. I don't want this stuff.
-How could…

263
00:15:38,074 --> 00:15:40,993
I'm incredibly sorry
if I hurt your pride,

264
00:15:41,577 --> 00:15:43,996
but you'll have to find someone else
to fawn over you.

265
00:15:44,664 --> 00:15:48,542
And since you're human,
you understand feelings.

266
00:15:48,626 --> 00:15:49,585
Right, Hijiri?

267
00:15:50,586 --> 00:15:53,130
And another thing,
there's no point strutting around

268
00:15:53,214 --> 00:15:55,299
promising my every wish
with your parents' money.

269
00:15:55,383 --> 00:15:57,802
It's okay when it's money
you earn yourself.

270
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:01,013
And above all…

271
00:16:03,140 --> 00:16:06,018
If you don't have Momohiki,
then you don't have a chance!

272
00:16:20,783 --> 00:16:22,535
That was interesting.

273
00:16:23,828 --> 00:16:25,162
Junta…

274
00:16:25,246 --> 00:16:27,832
If I had accepted Riri's conditions,

275
00:16:27,915 --> 00:16:31,002
would they have released Junta
from the love spell?

276
00:16:33,337 --> 00:16:35,089
I'm sorry you're involved with this.

277
00:16:35,673 --> 00:16:37,550
Don't be. I'm just fine.

278
00:16:38,884 --> 00:16:41,554
If you're ever in trouble,
please just let me know.

279
00:16:46,142 --> 00:16:48,060
He's too good of a person
it's painful.

280
00:16:51,939 --> 00:16:54,942
Hey Anzu, how come
you're playing with him anyway?

281
00:16:55,568 --> 00:16:57,653
Yeah, I won't let you play my new game.

282
00:16:59,113 --> 00:17:01,073
What? You suck.

283
00:17:01,157 --> 00:17:05,661
-Uh, are you sure?
-It's okay. Those guys are all talk.

284
00:17:07,079 --> 00:17:09,331
And I had plans to hang with you first.

285
00:17:10,666 --> 00:17:12,835
How come you kicked him out, huh?

286
00:17:12,918 --> 00:17:14,587
I really want to kick you out.

287
00:17:14,670 --> 00:17:16,630
Not nice!

288
00:17:17,673 --> 00:17:19,425
DONUTS

289
00:17:22,053 --> 00:17:25,556
Miss Hoshino,
we've got a new employee starting today.

290
00:17:25,639 --> 00:17:26,766
Oh, right.

291
00:17:28,059 --> 00:17:28,976
What?

292
00:17:29,894 --> 00:17:31,145
This is Mr. Koganei.

293
00:17:33,314 --> 00:17:36,025
Yes, I'm here to learn.
You should have no issues.

294
00:17:36,567 --> 00:17:38,486
CONBINI MART
SEASONAL SWEETS

295
00:17:39,361 --> 00:17:40,446
Welcome in.

296
00:17:44,533 --> 00:17:45,993
I appreciate that.

297
00:17:48,245 --> 00:17:49,121
Come again.

298
00:17:49,705 --> 00:17:51,791
Hey!

299
00:17:51,874 --> 00:17:53,834
How many meters above us are you?

300
00:17:53,918 --> 00:17:55,795
Excuse you, millions of meters.

301
00:17:56,462 --> 00:17:57,797
Orbitally higher?

302
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:00,341
You think that's good customer service?

303
00:18:00,966 --> 00:18:01,801
She's right.

304
00:18:02,593 --> 00:18:04,053
It's better if you add,

305
00:18:04,136 --> 00:18:07,306
"But I won't actually wait for you"
after "Come again."

306
00:18:07,389 --> 00:18:09,809
Don't encourage the hot and cold thing!

307
00:18:11,060 --> 00:18:13,604
Manager, sir, are you sure about this?

308
00:18:13,687 --> 00:18:15,815
Hmm, well, thing is…

309
00:18:16,941 --> 00:18:19,193
-Shall I warm it?
-Oh, yes.

310
00:18:19,276 --> 00:18:22,530
The customers all seem
to be attracted to Mr. Koganei's aura,

311
00:18:22,613 --> 00:18:24,115
so there haven't been any complaints.

312
00:18:24,198 --> 00:18:26,826
But he's inconsiderate and obnoxious!

313
00:18:28,744 --> 00:18:32,248
Hijiri went viral,
known as the convenience store prince.

314
00:18:32,331 --> 00:18:36,752
The #storeprince spread
like wildfire all over social media…

315
00:18:36,836 --> 00:18:38,295
SEASONAL SWEETS NOW AVAILABLE

316
00:18:38,379 --> 00:18:40,756
…and attracted a whole lot of customers!

317
00:18:43,884 --> 00:18:45,219
Mm-hm.

318
00:18:46,345 --> 00:18:52,268
AVAILABLE NATIONWIDE

319
00:18:53,477 --> 00:18:55,271
Your change. Do come again.

320
00:18:55,354 --> 00:18:56,605
Thanks.

321
00:18:58,357 --> 00:19:00,693
I guess he must've ended up
with that attitude

322
00:19:00,776 --> 00:19:03,779
because everyone around him
seems to enable him.

323
00:19:04,488 --> 00:19:06,782
But he is a fast learner,

324
00:19:06,866 --> 00:19:09,118
and he doesn't ask for time off.

325
00:19:09,201 --> 00:19:11,537
-And to be honest, he does work hard.
-Welcome in.

326
00:19:13,497 --> 00:19:15,374
-You can take your break now.
-Mm-hm.

327
00:19:17,293 --> 00:19:19,295
Wait, is the Prince going on break?

328
00:19:19,962 --> 00:19:22,298
Sorry about that.

329
00:19:22,381 --> 00:19:25,301
CONBINI MART

330
00:19:26,886 --> 00:19:29,805
I'm so tired.

331
00:19:29,889 --> 00:19:32,057
Oh, Mr. Tsuchiya.

332
00:19:34,643 --> 00:19:35,936
Good evening, miss.

333
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:38,439
Hi there. Hijiri will be out in a sec.

334
00:19:41,108 --> 00:19:42,067
Miss Hoshino.

335
00:19:42,568 --> 00:19:46,155
I don't know how to express the gratitude
I have for what you have done.

336
00:19:46,822 --> 00:19:47,823
What?

337
00:19:48,991 --> 00:19:53,579
Mr. Hijiri, he attended an expensive
escalator-styled private school,

338
00:19:53,662 --> 00:19:55,080
but due to his father's wishes,

339
00:19:55,164 --> 00:19:57,833
he was enrolled at the school
where you currently attend.

340
00:19:57,917 --> 00:19:59,084
Oh.

341
00:19:59,168 --> 00:20:01,003
His loved ones
are enamored with him,

342
00:20:01,086 --> 00:20:04,256
and he always got anything
and everything he wanted growing up,

343
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:06,926
so he can be a bit out of touch,
and he lacks common sense.

344
00:20:07,009 --> 00:20:07,843
Hmm…

345
00:20:08,636 --> 00:20:10,971
His father became concerned about that,

346
00:20:11,055 --> 00:20:13,140
so he decided that he wanted Hijiri

347
00:20:13,224 --> 00:20:15,809
to experience a normal life
at a normal school.

348
00:20:16,435 --> 00:20:19,313
However, his innate
and inherent heir of nobility

349
00:20:19,396 --> 00:20:21,857
has always made him feel
above everything normal.

350
00:20:22,942 --> 00:20:23,859
Right.

351
00:20:24,568 --> 00:20:28,447
But now, because you had the ability
to reason with him directly…

352
00:20:28,948 --> 00:20:32,368
First, I hit the bottom right key there.
And then I enter…

353
00:20:32,451 --> 00:20:37,289
Mr. Hijiri has actually been
trying to learn more about normal life.

354
00:20:39,041 --> 00:20:40,626
This is all your doing.

355
00:20:41,168 --> 00:20:42,628
Thank you so very much.

356
00:20:42,711 --> 00:20:44,255
Oh, of course.

357
00:20:49,218 --> 00:20:51,637
NARIKIN BANK

358
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:53,639
BANK ACCOUNT
ORDINARY FINANCIALS

359
00:20:55,224 --> 00:20:56,600
My paycheck!

360
00:20:57,184 --> 00:21:00,479
I'm so glad. How should I spend it? Hmm…

361
00:21:02,439 --> 00:21:04,275
Hoshino.

362
00:21:07,069 --> 00:21:10,114
Jeez, Hijiri!
There's no work today, is there?

363
00:21:10,197 --> 00:21:11,824
Then why are you following me?

364
00:21:11,907 --> 00:21:15,369
How rude. I just happened to see you
so I called your name.

365
00:21:16,078 --> 00:21:17,871
I received my paycheck today.

366
00:21:17,955 --> 00:21:20,582
So, Hoshino, what do you want?

367
00:21:21,166 --> 00:21:22,084
Huh?

368
00:21:22,167 --> 00:21:24,878
It's only a few days' worth
so it can't be too great,

369
00:21:24,962 --> 00:21:27,589
but I'm sure I can fulfill anything
your peasant heart desires.

370
00:21:28,590 --> 00:21:30,592
And I earned the money all on my own.

371
00:21:31,552 --> 00:21:33,595
But don't get the wrong idea.

372
00:21:37,433 --> 00:21:39,893
It's not like
I did any of this stuff for you.

373
00:21:40,602 --> 00:21:43,480
That hot and cold personality
was implanted in him.

374
00:21:44,148 --> 00:21:45,149
What do you want?

375
00:21:45,232 --> 00:21:48,319
-A bag? Some shoes?
-No, no, thanks.

376
00:21:48,402 --> 00:21:50,654
-Some jewelry?
-No, no, no, no.

377
00:21:50,738 --> 00:21:52,531
Instead of a gift,
would you prefer a date?

378
00:21:52,614 --> 00:21:53,490
Please, shut up!

379
00:21:53,574 --> 00:21:56,910
As much as I want to say
I don't want a thing from him…

380
00:22:02,750 --> 00:22:04,168
Hmm.

381
00:22:04,251 --> 00:22:07,421
Oh! All right, I know what I want.

382
00:22:13,510 --> 00:22:15,012
What in the world is that?

383
00:22:15,095 --> 00:22:17,014
Pipiko. You wouldn't know.

384
00:22:18,182 --> 00:22:20,976
It was surprisingly cheap,
even for a peasant's item.

385
00:22:21,060 --> 00:22:22,436
Hmm?

386
00:22:23,354 --> 00:22:24,938
Here. That's your half.

387
00:22:28,150 --> 00:22:29,943
Thank you for the treat.

388
00:22:30,778 --> 00:22:32,529
You're happy with something like this?

389
00:22:33,530 --> 00:22:36,533
Well yeah, I think it's the perfect thing
to share with friends.

390
00:22:44,833 --> 00:22:45,793
What do you think?

391
00:22:47,252 --> 00:22:49,380
It tastes artificial and cheap.

392
00:22:51,173 --> 00:22:53,092
But it's, it's not bad.

393
00:23:00,015 --> 00:23:00,849
What's wrong?

394
00:23:01,433 --> 00:23:03,852
Getting back my sanity. That's all.

395
00:23:07,398 --> 00:23:09,483
This might have been a huge mistake.

396
00:23:19,868 --> 00:23:22,204
I'm home, guys.

397
00:23:25,958 --> 00:23:26,959
What?

398
00:23:27,042 --> 00:23:27,876
ARISA
CAN WE MEET?

399
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:29,002
It's Kazuki's phone.

400
00:23:29,086 --> 00:23:30,379
ARISA
CAN WE MEET?

401
00:23:30,462 --> 00:23:34,383
It's a girl!

402
00:23:36,844 --> 00:23:38,595
A fanfare, please!

403
00:23:38,679 --> 00:23:40,681
And a big congratulations!

404
00:23:40,764 --> 00:23:43,058
Did you fall for my little trick?

405
00:23:43,142 --> 00:23:46,103
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

406
00:23:46,186 --> 00:23:49,857
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

407
00:23:49,940 --> 00:23:52,609
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

408
00:23:52,693 --> 00:23:54,987
Don't just let things be! Come on!

409
00:23:55,070 --> 00:23:57,739
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

410
00:23:57,823 --> 00:23:59,658
So I can make sure I get paid.

